// `Scriptor`'s mirror for audit 2026-10-03 finding 5: a `Lector` field.
//
// `Lector` was never open -- interface.inc gives it NO field rows, and its
// `.lector` arm in `__chk_ty_pre_member` lists only `lege_octeto` and
// `ab_introitu` -- so this program has always been `EXS-E0305`. It is here
// because the finding named both types and because the way it would reopen is
// the way `Scriptor` was open: someone adds a field row to `Lector` so that
// `l.descriptor` can be read, lists it in the arm, and gets the same
// lowering trap (exit 132) instead of a refusal. `exsc-exit=1` fails then.
//
// See ../scriptor_campus_occultus/ for the full account.

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    firma l = Lector.ab_introitu(a);
    firma x = l.descriptor;
    redde 0;
}
